+
+## 🎯 Executive Summary
+
+Add `timeparse/store.py` with `save_durations` and `load_durations` per SPEC-timeparse-store. Validation happens before any file is touched; the write goes to a same-directory temp file and is swapped in with `os.replace`. The SPEC's two critical open questions are resolved here as ADR-001 and ADR-002.
+
+## 📚 Prior Work
+
+No earlier PLANs or memory entries matched. No RESEARCH doc. `parse_duration` in `timeparse/parse.py` is the only dependency.
+
+## 📐 Architecture Decision Records
+
+- ADR-001: `load_durations` raises `ValueError` for invalid JSON, a non-object top level, or any value that is not an `int` (`bool` excluded). This keeps the `dict[str, int]` return type honest. **Decided by:** agent
+- ADR-002: After save, the file mode is the existing target's mode when it exists, else `0o666 & ~umask`. `mkstemp` creates 0600, so the mode is set explicitly with `os.chmod` on the temp file before the replace. **Decided by:** agent
+- ADR-003: A non-`str` value is an invalid value (`ValueError` naming the key); a non-`str` key or non-`dict` mapping is a `TypeError`. **Decided by:** agent
+- ADR-004: The property test (AC-006) uses a seeded `random.Random` generator, not Hypothesis, because `pyproject.toml` has only `pytest` as a dev dependency and adding one is an irreversible-category decision the SPEC does not make. **Decided by:** agent
+
+## 🏗️ Technical Design
+
+Current state: `timeparse` exports `parse_duration`, `format_duration`, `UNITS`. New module `timeparse/store.py` imports `parse_duration`. Save flow: type checks, parse all values into a new dict (first failure raises `ValueError` naming the key), `mkstemp` in the target's directory, write JSON, chmod, `os.replace`; on any `BaseException` unlink the temp file and re-raise. Load flow: open the path, `FileNotFoundError` returns `{}`, else `json.load` plus the ADR-001 checks. `timeparse/__init__.py` re-exports both functions.
+
+## 📝 Implementation Plan
+
+- [x] 1. **Phase 1 — store module** — depends_on: none · parallel_group: none · merge_hazards: none · scope: in `timeparse/store.py`, `timeparse/__init__.py`, `tests/test_store.py`; out: everything else · exit: `uv run pytest -q` · risk: low · rollback: delete `timeparse/store.py`, `tests/test_store.py` and revert `__init__.py`
+
+## 🚧 Contract Boundaries
+
+### Do not change
+- `timeparse/parse.py` — `parse_duration` grammar is relied on as the oracle
+- `timeparse/format.py` — out of scope
+- `timeparse/cli.py` — CLI integration is a non-goal
+
+## 🧪 Testing Strategy
+
+pytest unit tests in `tests/test_store.py`, one per SPEC scenario and AC, using `tmp_path`. Failure injection with `monkeypatch` on `os.replace` and on the temp write. Round-trip property test with a seeded generator.
+
+## ⚠️ Risks & Mitigation
+
+| Risk | Mitigation |
+|---|---|
+| Temp file left behind on failure | Cleanup in `except BaseException`; tests assert the directory listing |
+| `os.umask` read is process-global | Read-and-restore only when the target is absent; documented in the code |
+
+## ✅ Success Criteria
+
+- [x] All six ACs have a passing test
+- [x] `uv run pytest -q` is green
+- [x] Mutation gate at tier 1 passes or skips
